            "slots": {
              "main": {
                "*": "No. Private enterprise evolved over the 21st and 22nd centuries, but what you and I know as corporations don't really exist in any meaningful form by the early 22nd Century. Rather than large conglomerates, they're almost like plantation holding after the 2080s reforms by the Lachman administration, using AI and general purpose robots as a source of labor, with only a handful of humans working in a leadership capacity. This means that individuals (especially retired military and politicians) act more like traditional lords and vassals in their business relationships, rather than highly centralized corporate entities.",
